 'illustrative_conservative_widths':rows,
 'many_cell_note':'For M approximately independent cells, the largest Gaussian-scale fluctuation is O(sqrt(log M/N)); if N/log M -> infinity the entire shape-phase cloud collapses. Rescaling by sqrt(N) produces an internal fluctuation variable, not a fixed-extent new spatial circle.',
 'conclusion':'The two shape phases are legitimate internal continuous observables but fail the present DIM-SOURCE criterion for an additional macroscopic relational coordinate on the sharp-cell limit.',
